---
layout: layouts/product.njk
title: "Numbers"
description: "Local, toll-free, mobile, and ported numbers with E911 provisioning, CNAM and LIDB caller name, caller-ID services, and VoiceTel product integration."
---
{%- from "partials/v2/macros.njk" import arrow %}
{%- set localDid = pricingRuntime | volumeRate("did-local", 2000) %}
{%- set tollFreeDid = pricingRuntime | volumeRate("did-tollfree", 2000) %}

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
	"@context": "https://schema.org",
	"@type": "Service",
	"serviceType": "Phone number provisioning and porting",
	"name": "VoiceTel Numbers",
	"provider": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "{{ site.brand }}", "url": "{{ site.url }}" },
	"areaServed": "US",
	"url": "{{ site.url }}/numbers/",
	"description": "Local, toll-free, and mobile phone number provisioning and porting with per-number E911 provisioning, CNAM and LIDB caller name, and caller-ID services."
}
</script>

<section class="hero hero--page" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
	<div class="hero__bg" aria-hidden="true"></div>
	<div class="container hero__inner">
		<div class="hero__copy">
			<p class="eyebrow">Numbers</p>
			<h1 id="hero-heading">Numbers that connect the world.</h1>
			<p class="lede">Provision new numbers, port existing inventory, configure emergency-service records, and attach numbers to VoiceML, SIP trunks, hosted PBX, messaging, and lookup workflows.</p>
			<div class="cta-row">
				<a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="/signup/">Sign up {{ arrow(14) }}</a>
				<a class="btn btn--ghost btn--lg" href="/pricing/#did-local">See number pricing</a>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="hero__visual">
			{%- set panel = {
				title: "Number search example",
				tabs: ["Local", "Toll-free", "Mobile", "Area 212", "+ port-in"],
				active: 0,
				items: [
					{ num: "+1 (212) 555-0148", tag: "New York · NY", price: localDid, star: "/mo*" },
					{ num: "+1 (212) 555-0220", tag: "New York · NY", price: localDid, star: "/mo*" },
					{ num: "+1 (212) 555-0391", tag: "New York · NY", price: localDid, star: "/mo*" },
					{ num: "+1 (800) 555-3201", tag: "Toll-free", price: tollFreeDid, star: "/mo*" }
				],
				footnote: "* Per number per month at the 2K-DID volume tier."
			} %}
			{% include "partials/v2/list-panel.njk" %}
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tint" id="services" aria-labelledby="services-heading">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="section__head">
			<p class="eyebrow">Number services</p>
			<h2 id="services-heading">Local, toll-free, mobile, and ported numbers, with the records to go with them.</h2>
			<p class="lede">Provision or port, then attach E911 addresses, LIDB caller name, and inbound CNAM per number, from the numbering API or the portal.</p>
		</div>
		{%- set features = [
			{ icon: "hash", title: "Local DIDs", body: "Use local numbers for inbound voice, outbound caller ID, PBX users, and application workflows." },
			{ icon: "phone-vibrate", title: "Toll-free and mobile", body: "Support number types based on availability, compliance, and product eligibility." },
			{ icon: "arrow-right-circle", title: "Porting", body: "Move existing numbers with coordinated paperwork, validation, test windows, and cutover communication." },
			{ icon: "person-vcard", title: "CNAM, LIDB, and caller ID", body: "Set the outbound caller name your numbers display through LIDB: up to 15 alphanumeric characters per number, applied on VoiceTel's switch and submitted to the LIDB network. Turn inbound CNAM lookup on or off per number." },
			{ icon: "shield-check", title: "E911", body: "Associate your phone number with a validated service address so calls can be routed to the correct emergency response center. We support address assignment, validation, and detect errors by allowing testing that does not affect emergency services." },
			{ icon: "code-slash", title: "Numbering API", body: "Lifecycle control over phone numbers &mdash; search, order, provision, port, E911, LIDB caller name, messaging enablement, lookup, and inbound routing &mdash; across voice and messaging workflows without manual carrier coordination." }
		] %}
		{% include "partials/v2/feature-grid.njk" %}
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section section--white" id="porting" aria-labelledby="porting-heading">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="row row--reverse">
			<div class="row__text">
				<p class="eyebrow">Porting</p>
				<h2 id="porting-heading">Porting that doesn't lose customers mid-cutover.</h2>
				<p class="lede">Number portability is where most carrier migrations actually fail. Every port runs the same five steps, with the E911 record reissued before the port completes, not after.</p>
				<div class="cta-row">
					<a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/support/voice/porting/procedure/">Porting procedure</a>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="row__visual">
				{%- set steps = [
					{ title: "Eligibility check", body: "Against LERG and the losing carrier's portability rules." },
					{ title: "LOA preparation and submission", body: "Losing-carrier-side coordination handled by VoiceTel." },
					{ title: "Test window scheduling", body: "Calls to the number reach both the old and new endpoints during the window, so you can prove answer rates before cutover." },
					{ title: "Defined rollback path", body: "If the port lands and something breaks, we put it back inside business hours." },
					{ title: "E911 record reissued", body: "Before the port completes, not after." }
				] %}
				{% include "partials/v2/step-list.njk" %}
			</div>
		</div>

		<h3 class="subsection-heading">Numbers FAQ</h3>
		{%- set faqs = [
			{ q: "Can I port my number to your service?", a: "Yes. We can port most North American phone numbers, provided the number is eligible for porting. If your number is portable, we can help transfer it to our service." }
		] %}
		{% include "partials/v2/faq.njk" %}

		<div class="cta-band">
			<div class="cta-band__text">
				<h3 class="cta-band__title">Bring the numbers, keep the customers.</h3>
				<p class="cta-band__body">Open an account and we'll model the port timeline against your business calendar before any LOA gets signed.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="cta-band__actions cta-row">
				<a class="btn btn--primary" href="/signup/">Free trial {{ arrow(14) }}</a>
				<a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/pricing/#did-local">See number pricing</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
